DESCRIPTION = ("Computes p = i*j mod 113 from tokens (i, j, 113), read at the last position. "
 "Stage 1: each of the two content tokens is a lookup code (8-dim table over the 113 tokens): the position-0/1 embeddings are "
 "a token code plus a constant position vector, and token identity is recovered by nearest code. "
 "Stage 2: attention mixes the two token codes into a residual stream (resid_mid) that is additive in the two tokens (mean + a(i) + b(j)), "
 "which is what makes the MLP able to compute the product. "
 "Stage 3: the MLP maps that to a 9-dim product code that depends only on p = i*j mod 113 (mlp_post is the codebook entry of p). "
 "Stage 4: the readout is linear in that code: logits = c + code @ M. All tables were measured on the network.")
